 bioassays and each of these  three slides is configured the same way  the 12 residential sites are shown there  you'll see that there's these five four  neighborhoods cough larp mws and tbs  and then there's the one undeveloped  site which is from that state park  robert lewis-stevenson park and then on  the far right is the positive control  and on the far left is the negative  control  and the stars the asterisks on this plot  indicates statistically significant  difference uh from the uh negative  control  and so what we see is that first there's  no systematic difference between the  undeveloped sites and the residential  sites if anything the the most active  sample is is one of our undeveloped  sites uh but there are several of the  residential sites that have  elevated activity both with respect to  cytochrome p450 and with respect to aero  hydrocarbon receptor  agonism  there are far fewer statistically  significant effects in the il-8 and  cox-2 assays but there were a couple of  sites and the same sites that we saw  previously  as being  highly elevated for ahr and sip1a1  and then the third pair  is the estrogen receptor and androgen  receptor assays and  in this slide the positive control is  not shown because as you'll see the  bioassay responses are much smaller and  quite a number of them are negative this  is that antagonistic effect that i was  discussing earlier and so when we see a  negative response like this what it  means is that there's some leftover  testosterone or  estradiol in the system and the presence  of the extract is actually suppressing  that compared to the controls  now these bioassays  were highly intercorrelated with each  other and this totally makes sense  because the the cox2 and the il-8 and  the sip1a1 are all mediated through the  aero hydrocarbon receptor  and even though these assays were done  in different labs the red  shaded areas show us the strong  statistically significant positive  correlation between the  the hr