unds the red  spectral lines are the in silico  predicted fragments and the  black lines are the accurate mass  fragments measured in this  in this msms experiment that we  performed  between the inability to get a targeted  msns result for  these  samples  so there were many compounds we could  not obtain a targeted msms result for  and among the ones that we did get a  targeted msms there was often not enough  abundance to do very much with so  further efforts to concentrate select  purify would be helpful here and we're  working on  improving this set of the results  so where are we headed uh from here  first  we've proven that there are many things  in urban wildfire samples that were not  present in undeveloped  samples but based on the set of  bioassays we chose to apply here there's  not a systematic difference that that  those residential samples are more  bioactive and we also did not see any  systematic presence of the kinds of  compounds that you would see in a  typical environmental contaminants  database that is after this fire we  don't see a lot of residue of known  pesticides or known solvents  what we're seeing is  highly con  converted compounds that have been you  know subject to combustion  i think we can say that in this project  the gc  pathway yielded more success in  isolating and annotating compounds that  were related to the bio essay endpoints  and so for this purpose it was more  successful that  for other purposes it may not be  the same result obviously and then  there's the fundamental question about  whether we pick the right bioassays  there are many many different biological  endpoints that might be of concern and  it may be that the ones that we selected  are not the ones that we most need to  worry about and that's the challenge for  our toxicologists collaborators to  figure out what the right suite of  assays is to apply to these kinds of  samples  so i wanted to acknowledge the sources  of funding for this work  we had two  nih